From Green Fields to AI Feeds – My Story

I was raised in a village where the only constant notifications were the chirping of birds—each one with its own ringtone. Surrounded by greenery, fields, and crops, nature was my first classroom.

While other kids played with toys, I dissected mine. Electric toys didn’t survive more than two days—I had to see what magic was inside. I even opened our giant CRT TV once… not to fix it, just to figure out what made it glow like that!

Though I started learning computers a bit late, my curiosity didn’t waste time. I began by building websites—simple at first, but powerful in purpose. And today, I'm diving into the world of AI—developing smart agents using Copilot Studio and integrating them into our systems.

From field wires to website wires and now AI neurons—my journey proves one thing: when curiosity meets code, stories like mine are bound to happen.
